Z||000000||bHooper||10-29-2000||09:11 PM||||i have dissmantled my <B>Entire</B> suspension, in anticipation of my soon to arive poly bushings.<P>i also plan to replace the bearings (front/rear), stearing damper, ball joints, and the rear brakes.<P>things i am considering replacing are; the rack, front sway bar, and the springs.<P>as for the tie rod ends, i do not know how to tell if they are bad.  they have some play, but are difficult to move in any direction (herkyjerky).  does that mean they are shot?  the grease fittings look "ok", as do the boots.  but i am suspicious of this movement.<P>thanks!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-29-2000||09:35 PM||||If they are binding, which it sounds like yours are, they are shot. Good ones should move smoothly with some drag, even when fully greased.||||reg||1
